<title>LITHUANIA: C.BANK SAYS NO REPO AUCTION THIS WEEK.</title>
<headline>C.BANK SAYS NO REPO AUCTION THIS WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania's central bank said on Wednesday that it decided not to hold a repo auction this week.</p>
<p>&quot;Commercial banks have excess liquid funds at the moment but that does not mean that the situation will not change in the near future,&quot; the head of the bank's policy department Gitanas Nauseda told Reuters.</p>
<p>He also said that 10 out of 12 banks in the country signed up for repo auctions with the central bank.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 22 35 17</p>
</text>
